  "description": "The \u0027dss_meanings_cached\u0027 dataset is designed to facilitate the mapping and understanding of various column names within a data system. It includes key information such as unique identifiers, labels, detectability, data types, normalization modes, and additional descriptions. This dataset is particularly useful for data engineers and analysts who need to ensure data consistency and proper interpretation across different datasets. By providing a unique identifier for each column name, along with a corresponding label, the dataset helps in maintaining a clear mapping and identification system. The \u0027detectable\u0027 column indicates whether a column can be detected, which is crucial for data processing workflows. The \u0027type\u0027 column specifies the data type, aiding in the correct interpretation of data. The \u0027normalizationMode\u0027 column describes any normalization applied, ensuring data consistency. Lastly, the \u0027description\u0027 column offers additional context, enhancing the understanding of each column\u0027s role and significance. This dataset is essential for maintaining data integrity and facilitating efficient data management processes.",
